From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: win32u: the Windows font smoothing setting decides, not fontconfig

Text was drawn greyscale whatever Windows' font smoothing setting said:
win32u took each font's anti-aliasing from the host's fontconfig first
(font->aa_flags, from FC_ANTIALIAS/FC_RGBA), and only fell back to
HKCU\Control Panel\Desktop's FontSmoothing/FontSmoothingType when fontconfig
had no opinion. Debian's fontconfig says rgba "none" for every font, so
ClearType could never be turned on -- nor smoothing turned off -- from the
Control Panel or by SystemParametersInfo(SPI_SETFONTSMOOTHING*), which is
how Windows programs and settings change it.

When the Windows setting is present, it decides: ClearType draws subpixel
text in its orientation, standard smoothing greyscale, off two-colour. A
font's LOGFONT quality (NONANTIALIASED/ANTIALIASED/CLEARTYPE_QUALITY) still
overrides it, as on Windows, and a prefix with no setting keeps Wine's
fontconfig behaviour.

Gate: test/theme-gate.sh renders text under a fontconfig that forces
greyscale and requires colour fringes for ClearType, grey only for
standard, and two colours only for off.
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/font.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/font.c
@@ -193,6 +193,9 @@
 };
 
 static UINT font_smoothing = GGO_BITMAP;
+/* The Windows font smoothing setting (Control Panel\Desktop) is present:
+ * it decides, not the host's fontconfig preference for each font. */
+static BOOL font_smoothing_configured;
 static UINT subpixel_orientation = GGO_GRAY4_BITMAP;
 static BOOL antialias_fakes = TRUE;
 static struct font_gamma_ramp font_gamma_ramp;
@@ -4689,7 +4692,7 @@
 
         if (font)
         {
-            if (!*aa_flags) *aa_flags = font->aa_flags;
+            if (!*aa_flags && !font_smoothing_configured) *aa_flags = font->aa_flags;
             if (!*aa_flags)
             {
                 if (lf.lfQuality == CLEARTYPE_QUALITY || lf.lfQuality == CLEARTYPE_NATURAL_QUALITY)
@@ -4847,7 +4850,8 @@
                 break;
             }
         }
-        if (get_key_value( key, "FontSmoothing", &val ) && val /* enabled */)
+        if (get_key_value( key, "FontSmoothing", &val )) font_smoothing_configured = TRUE;
+        if (font_smoothing_configured && val /* enabled */)
         {
             if (get_key_value( key, "FontSmoothingType", &val ) && val == 2 /* FE_FONTSMOOTHINGCLEARTYPE */)
                 font_smoothing = subpixel_orientation;
